ae9b4df766a2f07b1d80c5ea905293426460e3c2  Apps/AllnighterMac/Sources/GUIProofGrantView.swift  # GUIProofGrantView renders the interactive one-time macOS Screen Recording grant flow and is STRUCTURALLY UNCAPTURABLE by gui_proof.sh, not merely untested: it mounts only when RootView sees GUIFixture.isGrantSession, that session name ('proof-grant') is absent from the benchScenarios fixture catalog, and GUIFixture.captureAndExitIfRequested() opens with 'guard isActive, !isGrantSession else { return }' so the self-capture path is explicitly skipped for it. No PNG can ever be produced. It is reachable only via the human-driven scripts/gui_proof_grant.sh. Contents: full-screen headline, explainer, live granted/not-granted status label, four numbered steps, a selectable app-path box, and Register-with-macOS / Open-System-Settings / Check-again / Quit buttons. To retire this waiver, add a non-interactive fixture that mounts the grant view without the TCC round trip. (2026-08-15)
ced40d0a69de07871e410223c6df148f22a728a0  Apps/AllnighterMac/Sources/AboutUpdatesView.swift  # AboutUpdatesView has NO REGISTERED FIXTURE. GUIFixture.swift carries routing for '.about' wired to settings-about-updates / studio-about-updates (lines ~117, ~157) but NEITHER NAME IS REGISTERED in the benchScenarios catalog, so neither is runnable — the routing is dead code. This is an honest gap, not a clean bill of health: the view is genuinely unproven, not 'probably fine'. What it renders (verified by reading the source, not by looking at pixels): a scrollable single-column page, max-width 720 — header, a 'This build' version card (app + CLI identity + last-checked), either an app-update-available card or an up-to-date card, an optional CLI-update card, a PATH card, and a release-channel card. No popovers, no sheets, no dynamic-width lists, which is why it is low-risk to defer rather than block on. TO RETIRE THIS WAIVER: register settings-about-updates in the benchScenarios catalog so the existing dead routing becomes runnable, then render and review it. That is a small change and should be done in the next GUI round. (2026-08-15)
91550425fb810a99b04f511d67754e8d2992a74a  Apps/AllnighterMac/Sources/AllnighterMacApp.swift  # AllnighterMacApp has NO VIEW BODY OF ITS OWN and therefore cannot earn a capture-based proof. Verified after reviewing all 11 Home/Root captures: nothing in any render is specific to this file. It hosts the Window and MenuBarExtra scenes and sets .frame(minWidth: 1100, minHeight: 720); every pixel in a capture belongs to a view it hosts, each of which is proven or waived separately. MenuBarExtra content is not part of the main-window bitmap capture at all. This is a content-bound waiver, not a convenience one: if this file ever grows its own visible chrome, or if window sizing itself becomes reviewable, the waiver must be retired and a real proof taken. (2026-08-15)
